  "result": "Perfect! All 64 tests pass. I've added invoice numbering functionality to the project:\n\n**New file: `src/numbering.js`**\n- `nextInvoiceNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)` \u2014 calculates the next free invoice number\n  - Format: `INV-<year>-<counter>` (e.g., `INV-2025-0001`)\n  - Counter is 4 digits, zero-padded, resets each year\n  - Handles unordered input and year boundaries\n\n**Added to `src/invoices.js`:**\n- `issueInvoice(invoice, existingNumbers)` \u2014 assigns a number and marks invoice as issued\n  - Returns ok(newInvoice) with number assigned and status changed to 'issued'\n  - Returns NOT_DRAFT if invoice status isn't 'draft'\n  - Doesn't mutate the original invoice\n\n**Created `test/numbering.test.js`** with 10 tests covering:\n- Starting counters for new years\n- Incrementing and zero-padding\n- Filtering numbers from other years\n- Handling unordered input and year boundaries\n- Edge cases (large counters, etc.)\n\n**Added 6 tests to `test/invoices.test.js`** for issueInvoice covering:\n- Assigning numbers and status changes\n- Calculating next numbers from existing ones\n- Preserving invoice data\n- NOT_DRAFT error handling\n- No mutation of original invoices\n- Year boundaries\n\nAll 64 tests pass (48 previous + 16 new).",
